```Rule: Brute force | MITRE T1110.001 Password Guessing | Python rule: brute_force```
```Logic: >= 10 failed logins from one source IP inside any 5-minute sliding window```

```--- Linux SSH (auth.log / linux_secure) ---```
index=linux sourcetype=linux_secure "Failed password"
| rex "Failed password for (invalid user )?(?<user>\S+) from (?<src_ip>\d{1,3}(\.\d{1,3}){3})"
| sort 0 _time
| streamstats time_window=5m count AS failures_5m BY src_ip
| where failures_5m >= 10
| stats max(failures_5m) AS peak_failures dc(user) AS users_targeted values(user) AS users
        min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen BY src_ip host
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)

```--- Windows Security (Event ID 4625) ---```
index=wineventlog EventCode=4625
| sort 0 _time
| streamstats time_window=5m count AS failures_5m BY src_ip
| where failures_5m >= 10
| stats max(failures_5m) AS peak_failures values(user) AS users min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen BY src_ip host
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
